  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{L}_1$ be the length of the common chord of the curves $x^2+y^2=9$ and $y^2=8 x$, and $L_2$ be the length of the latus rectum of $y^2=8 x$, then:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7nQiN",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{L}_1>\\mathrm{L}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NTl2v",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{L}_1=\\mathrm{L}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eLupT",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{L}_1 < \\mathrm{L}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZD6YT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{L}_1}{\\mathrm{~L}_2}=\\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/guBkIvWc8OCBG-UFkYe_nMLP2i11gKYo1aCf6r3dyjY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nWe have\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x^2+(8 x)=9 \\\\\n&x^2+9 x-x-9=0 \\\\\n&x(x+9)-1(x+9)=0 \\\\\n&(x+9)(x-1)=0 \\\\\n&x=-9,1 \\\\\n&\\text { for } x=1, y=\\pm 2 \\sqrt{2 x}=\\pm 2 \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n&\\mathrm{~L}_1=\\text { Length of } \\mathrm{AB} \\\\\n&\\quad=\\sqrt{(2 \\sqrt{2}+2 \\sqrt{2})^2+(1-1)^2}=4 \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n&\\mathrm{~L}_2=\\text { Length of latus rectum } \\\\\n&=4 a=4 \\times 2=8 \\\\\n&\\mathrm{~L}_1 < \\mathrm{L}_2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
